+### 0B Codegen of group lists vs hand-written groups (F6)
+
+Owner decision 5 ("Goal: features as LEGO bricks"). Main criterion: merge conflicts when several agents add modules to
+one feature in parallel. The rule below is fixed before the run, so the measurement decides.
+
+- Harness `research/module-entries-2026-10/merge-experiment.mjs` builds a disposable Git repository in a temp directory
+  per run, in the decision-1 layout: feature `orders` with 12 modules, each `composition/<m>.declaration.ts` and
+  `composition/<m>.module.ts`; `composition/orders.group.ts` (one import per line and one member per line, sorted);
+  `tests/features/orders/orders.wiring.ts` (one pin per line, sorted); `composition/orders.contracts.ts` (one
+  descriptor per line; the feature map with one `| typeof X` per line).
+- Each run creates K branches from one base, K = 3, 6 and 10. Every branch adds one module (two files, its group
+  lines and its oracle line); half of them also add a contract; K/5 branches remove or rename a module. Names come from
+  a seeded word list, 10 seeds per K.
+- Variants: M1 hand-written, sorted insertion; M2 M1 plus `.gitattributes` `merge=union` on the group, wiring and
+  contracts files; G2 the group file generated from `composition/*.module.ts` names, ignored by Git and produced before
+  typecheck and tests; G3 G2 plus a hand-written per-module pin file `tests/features/orders/wiring/<m>.wiring.ts` that
+  the generator aggregates into the oracle part (imports only). M3 and G1 are dropped (G1 conflicts like M1 by
+  construction).
+- Protocol as our agents work: each branch first merges the current `main` locally (git default `ort`), resolves, then
+  merges into `main` with `--no-ff`, in a fixed order.
+- Record per variant and per file: share of merges with a textual conflict; share resolvable mechanically (keep both
+  lines, or rerun the generator); invalid merges (typecheck or import resolution fails after a clean merge, or a removed
+  line returns); files and commands per module add; build steps and CI jobs added; detection of a branch that adds a
+  module but forgets the group line (the layout checks' orphan check must fail in M*; impossible in G*).
+- Decision rule: codegen wins only if (a) G2 or G3 has at most half the conflicted-merge share of the best hand-written
+  variant at K = 6 and K = 10, every touched file counted, with zero invalid merges, and (b) its cost is accepted: a
+  generator step before every typecheck, test and editor session in every consumer, shipped as a vendored script or a
+  new CLI package (a new admission; a leaf package may not carry `bin`, dependencies or files outside `dist`,
+  `architecture/checks/leaf-package-admission.mjs`). Otherwise: hand-written groups plus the layout
+  checks' orphan check; M2's union attribute is recommended to consumers only if it halves conflicts against M1 with
+  zero invalid merges (union keeps both sides; a deleted line next to an added one can return, which the typecheck then
+  reports).
+- ASSUMPTION, my prediction and not evidence: M1 conflicts on adjacent sorted inserts in the group and wiring files, M2
+  removes most of them, G2 and G3 remove the group conflicts but keep the contracts conflicts, so codegen does not reach
+  half.
+- `merge=union` acts on local merges, which is how our agents bring `main` into a branch (never GitHub "Update
+  branch"). Whether GitHub's mergeability check honors it is unknown (ASSUMPTION) and does not matter for that flow.
